<title>BELGIUM: PARIS-AMSTERDAM THALYS LINE SEES MILLIONTH CLIENT.</title>
<headline>PARIS-AMSTERDAM THALYS LINE SEES MILLIONTH CLIENT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thalys, the high-speed train service linking Amsterdam to Paris, expects to receive its one millionth traveller on Saturday, five months after its June 2 launch, Belgian railway company NMNS-SNCB said on Thursday.</p>
<p>NMBS said in a statement that trips between Paris and Belgian cities made up 75 percent of Thalys traffic.</p>
<p>Thalys offers 13 trains between Paris and Brussels, for the journey last less than two hours.</p>
